			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Maintain submodule for CI/CD and hygiene alignment\n\nUpdate the Element subtree to commit 72c26dd7, specifically pulling in maintenance revisions for the Maintain component. Integrate the latest GritQL queries, CI/CD configurations, and repository hygiene scripts to align the build pipeline and automated quality checks with current ecosystem standards.\n\nThis update is strictly tooling-focused and introduces no changes to the core editor logic, dependencies, or runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "e347572d7f0bcd41d571cba934660d455e74ab7c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T21:44:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				126,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 10 submodules for performance optimization and IPC efficiency\n\nUpdate the `Element` submodule to `a934a1ae` to integrate a coordinated suite of performance enhancements and build optimizations across the Land Editor ecosystem.\n\n**Cocoon**: Enable production tree shaking and conditionally disable debug logging, reducing the `Main.js` bundle by ~10% (1.49MB → 1.33MB). Refactor the performance monitoring service to a zero-overhead shim, replace array reductions with O(1) Exponential Moving Average for latency tracking, and update the bootstrap watchdog polling to 5s with `unref` intervals.\n\n**Mountain**: Enable full diagnostic tracing and implement robust TTY detection to skip shell enhancements in interactive terminals. Introduce a high-frequency command filter in `WindServiceHandlers` to bypass OTLP spans and Echo submission for silent commands (e.g., `logger:*`, `storage`), significantly reducing CPU overhead during boot.\n\n**Wind**: Consolidate Layer composition using `Layer.mergeAll` to reduce intermediate object allocations from O(n) to O(1). Streamline Tauri IPC argument serialization and standardize production builds to strip console statements.\n\nUpdates to **Common**, **Echo**, **Output**, **Rest**, **SideCar**, **Sky**, and **Worker** align with build hygiene and architectural consistency. These changes enhance runtime efficiency and prepare the stack for intensive testing.",
			"SHA": "0a7c37e349089a03f8b635a56aad3c7937cd37c9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T01:10:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				126,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Cocoon and Sky for build refresh and IPC diagnostics\n\nUpdate the `Element` submodule to the latest revision to integrate targeted enhancements in the extension host pipeline and UI component layer.\n\n**Cocoon**: Regenerate all TypeScript compilation outputs in the `Target/` directory and update the `RouteManifest` timestamp. This synchronizes JavaScript bundles, source maps, and gRPC service definitions for the extension host sidecar.\n\n**Sky**: Instrument the `Bridge.ts` webview postMessage handler with diagnostic logging via `MountainIPCInvoke`. Capture lifecycle events including entry receipt, registry lookup state, dispatch attempts, and execution errors. Logs include ViewId and message metadata to facilitate debugging of IPC flows between the Astro UI and VS Code workbench webviews.\n\nThese changes ensure the extension host is ready for the upcoming testing phase while providing granular visibility into the UI-to-backend communication bridge without altering core dispatch logic.",
			"SHA": "66f1c648eae630d6456cc3e65543d43dde0a432b"
		}
	],
